# Code block line-picking

Hold **Ctrl** (or **Cmd**) and move the pointer over the blocks below. The
highlight must bracket exactly one logical line, and clicking must copy that
same line.

Code blocks wrap, so a long line occupies several visual rows. Its highlight
should be one tall band covering all of them — not a one-row band, and not a
band offset from the line it claims to be on.

## Wrapped lines among short ones

Lines 3 and 6 wrap. Check that lines 7–9 are still picked correctly: an error in
the earlier wrapped lines shows up as drift further down the block.

```js
const a = 1;
const b = 2;
const config = { retries: 5, timeout: 30000, backoff: 'exponential', onError: (e) => console.warn('request failed, retrying', e), headers: { accept: 'application/json' } };
const c = 3;

function describe(thing) {
  return `${thing.name} has ${thing.parts.length} parts, weighs ${thing.massKg}kg, and was last serviced on ${thing.servicedAt.toISOString()}`;
}

const d = 4;
const e = 5;
```

## Blank lines

A blank line is pickable too, and its band is one row tall like any other.

```py
first = 1

second = 2


third = 3
```

## Every line wraps

```text
alpha bravo charlie delta echo foxtrot golf hotel india juliett kilo lima mike november oscar papa
quebec romeo sierra tango uniform victor whiskey xray yankee zulu one two three four five six seven
eight nine ten eleven twelve thirteen fourteen fifteen sixteen seventeen eighteen nineteen twenty
```

## Single line, no wrap

```sh
echo hello
```
